{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require all data centre consultations to include environment & community groups",
        "additional_details": "Data centres have an enormous impact on their surrounding local areas, on water supplies, energy supplies, and carbon emissions. Yet we feel the Government has so far failed to consult environment and community groups on this issue, preferring to talk almost entirely to representatives of the technology firms themselves. In our view, this brings a clear and unacceptable bias into the policy process.",
        "background": "Ministers and senior civil servants involved in making policy about the siting of data centres must be required to include in their consultations meetings with representatives of environment and community groups.",
        "closed_at": null,
